Baseline behaviour
------------------

Without F8, every cloud call reaches the wire with full PII intact:
  Vehicle hex JSON, GPS tuples, owner email, and free-text driver
  notes flow verbatim through audit (which hashes them) and trace
  (which spans them) into the OpenAI / Anthropic adapters.

The redaction decorator MUST sit innermost so audit/trace observe
the post-redaction payload, not the original. The strategy hook
(RedactionPolicy()) already exists from F4; F8 wires its result
into a per-request ctx value that the decorator pulls.


=== REASONING ===

Why this design preserves ADR-015
---------------------------------

§I1 Default off
  The redact package is dormant in off mode: dispatch.Run is gated
  by guard.Wrap, so an off-mode request never reaches the line that
  installs the policy. Even with no policy in ctx, redact.DefaultPolicy
  is deny-all — the failure mode of a misconfigured strategy is
  MORE redaction, never less.

§I3 Feature-gated
  WithRedaction is unconditionally applied to the chain, but it is
  a NO-OP for off mode (the dispatcher never reaches the wire in
  off mode). For non-off mode, every Strategy declares its own
  Allow-list via RedactionPolicy(); a strategy that "forgets" to
  declare one inherits NoRedaction → DefaultPolicy → deny-all.

§I4 Zero outbound egress (hard invariant)
  This is F8's headline invariant. The decorator is the LAST
  cross-cut before the wire (innermost in the chain), so audit + trace
  see the post-redaction text. Three layers of defence:
    1. WithRedaction is INNERMOST in the chain order
       (provider.NewRegistry call site below).
    2. The decorator deep-copies req.Messages + req.Input into a
       fresh slice with fresh Message values — the strategy's
       original input is never mutated, so a re-tried call cannot
       "leak via re-redaction-with-different-policy".
    3. Manifest values (the original PII) live ONLY in process
       memory inside the meta sink; the sink is wiped on TTL
       (60s) and never serialised. The DB columns added by
       000207 hold class LABELS only ('vin','email',...), never
       values.

§I5 No raw SQL mutation outside repo
  The new redact code lives entirely in /internal/ai/redact and
  /internal/ai/provider. The single SQL insert is in the existing
  AICallLogRepo.Insert, parameterised, no string concatenation.

§I6 404 in off mode
  The new /api/v1/ai/admin/redaction-bypass endpoint is wrapped by
  adminGuardSettings inside mountAIAdminRoutes — a direct copy of
  the F3 __usage__ pattern. Off mode → 404 (verified by
  TestAdminGuardSettings_RedactionBypassTracksMode).

§I7 Per-feature opt-in
  The redact decorator runs for every /api/v1/ai/* call (it is
  in the chain), but its OUTPUT is governed by the per-strategy
  RedactionPolicy(). A new strategy that doesn't define the policy
  inherits NoRedaction (deny-all) — opt-OUT requires explicit
  Allow entries.

§I9 Privacy + redaction (this slice's headline invariant)
  Eleven PIIClass detectors (VIN, email, phone, latlong, address,
  IP, plate, CC, SSN, vehname, userid) cover the prompt's class
  list. Defaults: deny-all + RedactedTags mode (round-trippable
  via Restore). Manifest never persisted, never sent.

§I10 No silent network egress
  The decorator does not emit any new network call. The bypass
  report endpoint reads from ai_call_log only (no provider call).

§I12 Auditable
  Every cloud call now records (redacted_classes, redaction_bypass)
  in ai_call_log alongside the existing F3 audit fields. The
  bypass report endpoint surfaces aggregate bypass ratios per
  (feature, provider) so an operator can verify the deny-by-default
  stance held.

Why the redactadapter subpackage exists
---------------------------------------

The naive design imports `strategy` from `redact` (so
redact.PolicyAdapter can embed strategy.NoRedaction). But provider
imports redact (the decorator), and strategy imports provider
(strategies build provider chains). That closes a cycle:

  provider → redact → strategy → provider

Resolution: redact does NOT import strategy. A new tiny subpackage
internal/ai/strategy/redactadapter imports BOTH and provides the
bridge:

  type PolicyAdapter struct {
      strategy.NoRedaction          // satisfies strategy.RedactionPolicy
      Inner redact.Policy            // carries the F8 value
  }
  func Wrap(p redact.Policy) strategy.RedactionPolicy
  func From(sp strategy.RedactionPolicy) redact.Policy

This matches the "thin adapter package" pattern used elsewhere in
hexagonal Go and keeps the redact package free of any cross-cut.
Documented in the CHANGES section as an adaptation from the prompt's
allowed-files list.

Why migration slot 000207 (not 000202 as prompt says)
-----------------------------------------------------

Prompt 0009 hardcodes `migrations/000202_*`, but slot 000202 is
already taken by `ai_features_archive` from F2 (Phase-50 / 0003).
The next free post-AI-pipeline slot after 000206_embeddings (F7) is
000207. F3 set the precedent for documenting slot variance
(its prompt also said 000200, was bumped to 000201). Header comment
in the migration file calls this out explicitly.


