=== AI-OFF CONTRACT ===

Per ADR-015, every slice that touches an invariant MUST cite evidence.

  §I1 Default off
    EVIDENCE: redact.DefaultPolicy() returns Allow=nil, Bypass=false
              — strategy with no RedactionPolicy() override gets
              deny-all + apply-redaction. Test:
              TestPolicy_DefaultIsDenyAll in policy_test.go.
              Decorator never runs in off mode because dispatch.Run
              is gated upstream by guard.Wrap.

  §I3 Feature-gated
    EVIDENCE: WithRedaction wraps EVERY provider built by the
              registry, but the decorator's behaviour is governed
              by the per-strategy RedactionPolicy(). Strategies
              that forget to override inherit strategy.NoRedaction
              (default-deny). Wired in dispatch.Run line ~183:
                ctx = redact.WithPolicy(ctx, redactadapter.From(s.RedactionPolicy()))

  §I4 Zero outbound egress (HARD)
    EVIDENCE: Three layers of defence pinned by tests:
              1. Chain order: WithRedaction is FIRST argument to
                 provider.NewRegistry → INNERMOST at runtime →
                 closest to the wire. Verified by reading
                 internal/ai/provider/registry.go's Chain helper
                 (LIFO reduce).
              2. Decorator deep-copies req.Messages + req.Input
                 before mutating. Test: TestRedactDecorator_DoesNotMutateInput
                 in redact_decorator_test.go.
              3. Manifest values stay in process memory only.
                 Sink wiped on 60s TTL via opportunistic sweep.
                 Test: TestProcessMetaSink_TTLSweep in ctx_test.go.
              Migration 000207 stores class LABELS, never PII values
                 (verified by reading the COMMENT ON COLUMN strings
                 in the up.sql).

  §I5 No raw SQL mutation outside repo
    EVIDENCE: All SQL writes go through *AICallLogRepo.Insert
              (parameterised, $1..$N). New columns slotted into
              the existing INSERT statement; no string interpolation.

  §I6 404 in off mode
    EVIDENCE: TestAdminGuardSettings_RedactionBypassTracksMode pins
              that adminGuardSettings.AIFeatureEnabled returns false
              when the inner mode is "off", which guard.Wrap turns
              into a 404. Symmetric to the F3 __usage__ test.

  §I7 Per-feature opt-in
    EVIDENCE: RedactionPolicy() is a Strategy interface method.
              No Strategy registers itself outside the per-feature
              guard surface. The redact ctx value is set inside
              dispatch.Run AFTER strategy.Get(featureID) — so a
              strategy missing from the registry never gets a policy
              installed.

  §I9 Privacy + redaction (this slice's headline)
    EVIDENCE: Eleven PIIClass detectors in detect.go cover the
              prompt's class list (VIN, email, phone, latlong,
              address, IP, plate, CC, SSN + vehname, userid).
              Defaults: deny-all + RedactedTags (round-trippable).
              Manifest is process-local, TTL-swept, never persisted.
              Curated fixtures per class in detect_test.go.

  §I10 No silent network egress
    EVIDENCE: The redact decorator emits NO network call. The
              bypass report handler reads from ai_call_log only;
              no provider invocation. grep for "http\." or
              "Dial" in internal/ai/redact returns no matches.

  §I12 Auditable
    EVIDENCE: Migration 000207 adds redacted_classes TEXT[] +
              redaction_bypass BOOLEAN to ai_call_log. The repo's
              Insert consumes redact.ConsumeMeta(MetaKey(...)) and
              writes the values. The bypass report endpoint
              (/api/v1/ai/admin/redaction-bypass) surfaces
              per-(feature, provider) bypass ratios so an operator
              can verify the deny-by-default stance held over time.

  §I7 + Forward dependency
    EVIDENCE: Every existing Strategy (chatbot, digest, alert
              builder, automation builder, drive coaching) inherits
              strategy.NoRedaction by default. Strategies that opt
              into a more permissive policy use redactadapter.Wrap
              with one of the named policies in
              internal/ai/redact/policies.go. The bridge is
              explicit — silent permissive defaults are impossible.


